WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.542
Excuse me, sir.

00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:09.875
-What?
-We're hungry.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.417
I could eat.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.792
Surf Shop, Surfer Boy Pizza.
This is Argyle speaking.

00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:22.917
We make everything fresh
here at Surfer Boy,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.250
except for our pineapple,
which comes from a can.

00:02:13.792 --> 00:02:16.500
There's a 4 p.m. showing
of &lt;i&gt;Police Academy 3&lt;/i&gt;.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:18.625
Could be fun.

00:02:18.708 --> 00:02:20.917
Maybe we just
stay home today.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.125
What is this?

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.042
What, you guys just gonna
mope around all break?

00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:25.042
No one's moping.

00:02:25.125 --> 00:02:26.917
It's just the movie's
supposed to suck.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.708
-I was with my band.
-Corroded Coffin!

00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:43.167
-Corroded…
-Oh, my God. Yes.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.208
-You do remember.
-Of course.

00:02:44.292 --> 00:02:46.000
With a name like that,
how could I forget?

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.250
I don't know.
You're a freak.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.250
Parties,

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:52.667
or a game
where you toss balls

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.458
into laundry baskets!

00:02:54.542 --> 00:02:56.542
-Loser!
-You want something, freak?

00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:22.917
It's not exactly
the Ritz, is it?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.833
Right, &lt;i&gt;Doctor Zhivago&lt;/i&gt;.
It's a double VHS.

00:03:39.917 --> 00:03:41.083
It's long,

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.750
but that's because
it's filled with action

00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:45.958
and romance and
a little bit of suspense.

00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:47.083
Ozzy Osborne?

00:03:48.792 --> 00:03:49.792
Black Sabbath?

00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:52.750
He… He bit a bats head off.

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:54.750
-I don't--
-No? Doesn't matter.

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.333
Very metal, what you did.
That's all I'm saying.

00:04:12.417 --> 00:04:15.500
Did you know, peanut butter
is banned in motherland?

00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:18.042
I buy for
dollar-thirty here,

00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:20.167
sell for $20 there.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.292
Your mother must
be very proud.

00:04:26.208 --> 00:04:28.833
Someone has been
in my peanut butter.

00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:31.750
Very popular, as I said.

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:46.500
-Michael Myers.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:47.375 --> 00:04:48.375
Michael Myers.

00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:51.000
If you ask me,
Victor's like that.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.958
There's a real bogeyman.

00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:57.042
Is that what you call this?

00:04:58.542 --> 00:05:01.792
Did I survive?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.458
No, I assure you,

00:05:07.542 --> 00:05:10.375
I am still
very much in hell.

00:05:13.292 --> 00:05:15.833
-Hey, Steve…
-Did you guys see this?

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:17.542
-How many phones you have?
-Someone was murdered.

00:05:17.625 --> 00:05:19.708
How many phones do you have?

00:05:19.792 --> 00:05:20.708
We've got two. Why?

00:05:20.792 --> 00:05:22.500
Technically three, if you
count Keith's in the back.

00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:23.833
Yeah, three works.

00:05:37.542 --> 00:05:40.042
Okay, so I asked
for vomit green

00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:41.667
and I got vomit green.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.125
Isn't that awesome?

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.083
I said, turn it off.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:46.667
If you say so.

00:05:53.625 --> 00:05:54.875
Wipeout!

00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:12.875
My name is Lady Applejack,

00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:15.875
and I'm a chaotic good,
half-elf rogue, Level 14.

00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:18.375
And I will sneak behind
any monster you throw my way

00:06:18.458 --> 00:06:21.208
and stab them in the back
with my poison-soaked kukri.

00:06:21.292 --> 00:06:23.833
And I'll smile
as I watch them die

00:06:23.917 --> 00:06:26.208
a slow, agonising death.

00:06:26.292 --> 00:06:27.833
So, we gonna do this,

00:06:27.917 --> 00:06:29.375
or we gonna
keep chitchatting

00:06:29.458 --> 00:06:31.167
like this is your mummy's
book club?

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.250
You open for something
a little more challenging?

00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:56.083
-C?
-G?

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.208
-G, yeah. U…
-U…

00:06:58.292 --> 00:06:59.875
-A… R…
-A… R…

00:06:59.958 --> 00:07:01.250
"Guar"?

00:07:01.333 --> 00:07:02.625
"Guar…"

00:07:05.083 --> 00:07:06.208
&lt;i&gt;"Guar…"&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.792
-"Guard."
-"Guard."

00:07:07.875 --> 00:07:09.000
-Guarded.
-Guarded.

00:07:09.083 --> 00:07:11.500
Guarded, okay.
Watergate's guarded.

00:07:11.583 --> 00:07:13.458
Perfect, yes. Yes. Yes!

00:07:59.208 --> 00:08:01.083
Twelve Ricks already
have accounts here.

00:08:01.167 --> 00:08:02.458
-That's a lotta Ricks.
-Bingo.

00:08:02.542 --> 00:08:04.167
-Lipton?
-Spelled like the tea.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.417
2121 Holland Road.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.833
That's out by Lovers Lake.

00:08:06.917 --> 00:08:07.917
Middle of nowhere.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.625
It's a perfect
place to hide.

00:08:22.625 --> 00:08:25.417
Truly wonderful.
What an inspiring story.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.042
&lt;i&gt;We are all time-travellers&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;if you think about it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.875
&lt;i&gt;For example, this week&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;is going very fast,&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:34.792
&lt;i&gt;I think&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;because I am so busy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.625
&lt;i&gt;I have to make something&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;called a "visual aid".&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.542
&lt;i&gt;I hope Mrs. Gracie&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;will give me an A.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:44.000
I'm running
out of time here.

00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:46.042
Just hold your horsies,
Dusty-bun.

00:08:52.083 --> 00:08:54.375
-Do you see it?
-Yeah, I see it.

00:08:55.292 --> 00:08:57.042
-Yikes, Dusty.
-Yeah.

